{"title":"Forming plurals of irregular nouns","key_idea":"Some nouns change their spelling completely or follow special rules when they become plural, rather than just adding -s or -es.","method":["Look at the noun and check if it ends in a consonant + y, a vowel + y, -f, -fe, -ch, -sh, -x, -z, or -s.","If it ends in consonant + y, change y to i and add -es: for example, baby becomes babies.","If it ends in -f or -fe, change to -ves: for example, leaf becomes leaves.","If it ends in -ch, -sh, -x, -z, or -s, add -es: for example, box becomes boxes.","Some nouns are irregular and do not follow a pattern, so you must memorize them: for example, child becomes children."],"worked_example":{"problem":"Write the plural of: dish, knife, woman.","steps":["Dish ends in -sh, so add -es to get dishes.","Knife ends in -fe, so change -fe to -ves to get knives.","Woman is an irregular noun, so it becomes women (the vowel and ending change)."],"answer":"The plurals are dishes, knives, and women."},"key_terms":[{"term":"irregular noun","meaning":"a noun that does not follow the usual pattern when made plural"},{"term":"consonant + y","meaning":"a word ending where y comes after a consonant letter, like in baby"}],"common_mistakes":["Forgetting to change the -f in leaf to -ves, and writing leafs instead of leaves.","Treating child like a regular noun and writing childs instead of children."],"remember":"Consonant + y becomes -ies; -f or -fe becomes -ves; -ch, -sh, -x, -z become -es; some plurals must be learned by heart.","quick_check":[{"q":"Write the plural of wolf.","a":"Wolves (change -f to -ves)."},{"q":"Write the plural of boy.","a":"Boys (add -s because o is a vowel before y)."}],"tell_your_child":"Some words don't follow the usual rule when we make them plural, so you have to learn which ones are special. Look at how the word ends and decide which rule to use.","picture":{"concept_key":"c5-english-irregular-plurals","scene_prompt":"A child holding a stack of different objects: a box, leaves, and a young person beside them, all clearly visible and friendly."}}
